"reasoning": "The patient presents with leg swelling that causes shoes to feel tight and results in discomfort during prolonged sitting. These symptoms are classic indicators of venous insufficiency and varicose veins, where impaired blood return leads to fluid accumulation (edema) and aching in the lower limbs. Prolonged sitting worsens the condition by further impeding circulation. Other candidates like diabetes (typically presenting with excessive thirst, frequent urination, and fatigue) or arthritis (characterized by joint stiffness and pain during movement) are factually ruled out by the absence of their defining systemic or musculoskeletal features. The symptom profile directly matches the reference cases for varicose veins.",
"final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]varicose veins[/DIAGNOSIS]"
